> same 'average enchantment'.)

otmp->spe, as I noted, starts out as being whatever the object was
randomly assigned as part of the standard generation procedure. That's
in mksobj() in mkobj.c; for armour, the code is:

        case ARMOR_CLASS:
                if(rn2(10) && (otmp->otyp == FUMBLE_BOOTS ||
                   otmp->otyp == LEVITATION_BOOTS ||
                   otmp->otyp == HELM_OF_OPPOSITE_ALIGNMENT ||
                   otmp->otyp == GAUNTLETS_OF_FUMBLING ||
                   !rn2(11))) {
                        curse(otmp);
                        otmp->spe = -rne(3);
                } else if(!rn2(10)) {
                        otmp->blessed = rn2(2);
                        otmp->spe = rne(3);
                } else  blessorcurse(otmp, 10);

rne() is an exponential distribution: rne(3) has a 2/3 chance of
returning 1, 2/9 of returning 2, etc, capped at XL/3 or 5, whichever
is higher.

